# Which manager the Home Harness agent joins (home-harness-agent.service).
# The service stays off until this file has AGENT_ARGS filled in.
#
# Get the values from your manager's dashboard ("Add a device") or from
# `harnessctl join`. On the machine with the manager:
#   - the manager's address, e.g. 192.168.1.20:7420
#   - its certificate fingerprint (printed when the manager starts)
#   - the pairing token, or use -pair to be approved on the dashboard instead
#
# Example (replace every <...>; never publish a real token):
#   AGENT_ARGS="-manager-addr <host>:7420 -manager-fingerprint <fingerprint> -pairing-token <token>"
#   AGENT_ARGS="-manager-addr <host>:7420 -manager-fingerprint <fingerprint> -pair"
#
# This file holds a secret: keep it readable by root only (chmod 600).
# Then: sudo systemctl enable --now home-harness-agent
AGENT_ARGS=""
